messages:
maria: Heads-up — PR #1287 for the function/tool-calling docs is up for review. Main asks: update TypeScript SDK snippet, add a schema guardrail example, and fix the demo repo link. ping @sam @jay

sam: On my todo list. Quick Q — do we keep the old `response_schema` example or move everyone to the new `structured_output` pattern?

jay: Prefer `structured_output` for clarity. The v2 SDK changed the call pattern so the snippets need to show `client.tools.call(...)`. I can drop a short TS snippet.

maria: Great. Also we need a small guardrail example for required vs optional fields. e.g.:
```json
{"type":"object","properties":{"title":{"type":"string"},"summary":{"type":"string"}},"required":["title"],"additionalProperties":false}
```

olivia: From PM: users keep hitting parsing failures when models emit stray top-level fields. Can we include a fallback parsing pattern (lenient parse + validation) and a note about `additionalProperties`?

sam: I'll add a parse-shim snippet. Something like:
```ts
try {
  const parsed = JSON.parse(text);
  validate(parsed);
} catch (err) {
  // fallback: regex-based extraction or prompt-retry
}
```

jay: Also the demo repo link in the doc points to https://github.com/redwood-inference/tool-examples which is outdated. Should point to https://github.com/redwood-inference/examples/tree/main/tool-calling (or our docs-hosted examples path).

maria: I'll update the links. Small checklist for the PR: 1) update TS SDK snippet, 2) add guardrail example + explanation, 3) swap links, 4) add a tiny migration note, 5) add docs CI test that builds the example.

deploy-bot: Docs build check (main) — ✅ build passed, 1 warning in examples/migrations.md

sam: I can review after lunch. @jay can you paste the TS snippet here so I can copy it into the PR?

jay: Snippet: 
```ts
// v2 SDK tool call (TS)
const res = await client.tools.call('summarize', { input: prompt });
// structured_output: top-level `output` array with content objects
console.log(res.output?.[0]?.content);
```

maria: 👍 perfect, thanks. I'll commit that. Also added a short migration note to the doc: "Apps using freeform text outputs should migrate to structured outputs; see the snippet and guardrail section."

olivia: SGTM. Can we add a one-line note about possible token cost impact when using stricter guardrails? e.g., prompting for stricter structure can increase tokens used for retries/clarifications.

maria: Added: "Note: stricter schema prompts and validation may increase token usage; balance strictness with cost and UX."

sam: Left two inline comments on the PR: one about clarifying `required` semantics and another about avoiding prescriptive language (replace "must" with "recommended").

maria: Thanks — addressing those now. Plan is to merge EOD if no more blockers.

jay: Quick follow-up: do we want a tiny example of using a JSON schema validator in the SDK examples? I can add `ajv` usage in a separate snippet.

maria: Yes please — small `ajv` snippet under "post-parse validation" section would be great.

deploy-bot: Reminder: docs CI will block merge on build failure. Current status: all green.

sam: Reviewing now, will approve if inline comments resolved.

maria: Thanks everyone — will push remaining edits and ping when ready for final pass.
